{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZbdv5ZWMGJCWgGveSoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Controller implementation: `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — currently has create, get, and list endpoints\n- Entity model: `Shipment.kt:9-27` — immutable data class with status enum\n- Repository: `ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` — in-memory store with save/findById/existsById methods\n- Exception handling: `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- Error codes: `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum for machine-readable errors\n- Exception handler: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` — maps exceptions to ApiError responses\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Errors are thrown from controllers/services, caught centrally by GlobalExceptionHandler\n2. ConflictException returns HTTP 409; ResourceNotFoundException returns HTTP 404\n3. Repository methods are injected and called from controller\n4. Tests use MockMvc with `.andExpect(status()...)` and `.andExpect(jsonPath()...)` patterns\n5. POST endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(saved)` on success\n6. Error responses use ErrorCode enum values\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add the POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` — must add error code for invalid state transitions (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for the confirm endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if status handling is wrong\n- Not implementing idempotent retry behavior (must succeed without error on re-confirmation)\n- Using incorrect HTTP status codes\n- Missing or incorrect error code in the enum\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket specifies all required behaviors clearly.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code to enum for 409 conflicts when confirming a CANCELLED shipment or invalid transitions.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID (throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found)\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and persists it\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent retry)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - Returns the shipment as ResponseEntity.ok().body(shipment)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test methods:\n   - Confirm a CREATED shipment → returns 200 with CONFIRMED status\n   - Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment → returns 200 unchanged (idempotency)\n   - Confirm a CANCELLED shipment → returns 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - Confirm a non-existent shipment → returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered adding the confirm logic to the repository layer (e.g., `repository.confirm(shipmentId)`), but the current architecture has validation and error handling in the controller layer, so I'll follow that pattern. Keeping logic in the controller maintains consistency with the existing create() endpoint, which also performs validation and status management before calling save().\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Status |\n|------|------|-------|----------|--------|\n| Confirm CREATED | repository.findById(id) | repository.save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | Shipment | 200 |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED | repository.findById(id) | none | Shipment | 200 |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | repository.findById(id) | none | ConflictException | 409 |\n| Confirm missing | repository.findById(id) returns null | none | ResourceNotFoundException | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Happy path — confirm a newly created CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: Idempotency — confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment returns 200 with no change\n- Test 3: Invalid state — confirm a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 conflict\n- Test 4: Missing resource — confirm a non-existent shipment returns 404 not found\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":984,"cache_read_input_tokens":18981,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":984},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62111b27-d491-4275-b5a4-60a60835a9b0","uuid":"d039b7a2-9430-4e93-961e-552ed3a09404","timestamp":"2026-09-30T12:08:53.026Z","request_id":"req_011CfZbduLAqP2BbBzzp2r1m"}
